MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=9
DESCRIPTION=Issue 384 follow-up. D9: one header-only fl_sqlite_exec and fl_sqlite_ensure_columns (validated identifiers, fail-closed probe, stderr on bad table name) replace the copies in user_db.c, bridge.c, net_wifi_db.c and server_shared_db.c; a failed undo rolls back a transaction the helper opened, every exec failure is named on stderr, and the tests pin the limits, the probe error and the released savepoint. D7: one bounded big-endian codec in net_codec.h replaces the hand-shifted put/get in net_file_delivery.c and the kq_w_t/kq_r_t reader in net_kq_delivery.c, with null-buffer and sticky null-read hardening, one sticky writer for KQ frames and all-or-nothing bytes16 puts and gets; wire bytes unchanged; test_kq_wire links kq_driver.o once. D14: local VFS text and byte writes stage via fl_fs_stage_file and refuse symlink destinations, and a replaced file keeps its permission bits; the checkpoints stay on the fl_fs_* placement layer (the counterpart of KeyQuorum's Storage trait) that the provider itself builds on, by design, and that layering is documented. D11: fl_kq_driver_get returns the static KeyQuorum driver only when the registry contains it and the file ABI probe succeeds; one fl_kq_driver_get_or_register (atomic fl_driver_registry_ensure, refused after drivers_shutdown) replaces four registration copies; fl_kq_driver_get is now the one resolver in driver_model.c (registered pointer under the model lock, ABI re-probed), shared by the native shell and the lab. D8: catalog import refuses a symlinked blobs directory even with zero rows; revoke returns FL_RESULT_NOENT for reserved and unknown transfer IDs; the KeyQuorum host store is now FL_CHANNEL_PAYLOAD_KQ rows of the host catalog (kq_delivery.db and kq_spike removed, history in catalog_event, one transaction per co-sign and release, expired rows kept so an id is held once, released letters expire after 24 h), through one shared catalog file core (server_catalog_file.c); server file inbox and sent list co-signed deliveries, and an older build's kq_delivery.db is carried into the catalog once. D15: the KeyQuorum event and outcome names come from KeyQuorum's own kq_file_event_name and kq_file_outcome_name (files ABI 2, pin 4d20969) through two driver operations, and the C name tables are gone; a test still pins every code. D6: the 4 MiB copy-backup cap of fl_fs_commit_files is asserted. D13: every KeyQuorum buffer, store handle and part buffer is MEM_DOMAIN_FS memory, and the file readers that fill an fl_kq_buf_t (fl_fs_read_file and its _in/_at forms) allocate there too, so one release path (fl_kq_buf_free or mem_domain_free) covers them; the binaries that link the readers now link mem_domain.o. Review fixes (QA and Security team check): a failed restore in fl_fs_commit_files keeps the backup that holds the original; the KeyQuorum landing checks its destination with fl_server_shared_resolve_local_path before decoding; a password-hash working copy is secure-zeroed; a replaced file takes only its permission bits, not setuid or setgid. Owner-decision items aligned with KeyQuorum: a catalog file that cannot be tightened to owner-only now fails to open (src/db/mod.rs restrict_owner_only); expired deliveries keep their history and lose only the payload, as KeyQuorum's tombstones do. DevOps skill: human authorization before Orchestrator push, team sizing, seat rotation, per-Coder detached worktrees, and integrated-tree QA refuses any seat in the cumulative author set.


RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-29
